# Found incidentally while building tests/pty_test_helpers.crush (see its own header
# comment): `source`-ing (or `execute::file`-ing) a file with 3 or more top-level
# statements, from within an already-running script, deadlocks -- reproduces with
# plain `echo` statements, nothing pty-specific about it. Root cause suspected (not
# fixed here, out of scope for the plan that found this): `execute::file`'s shared
# output pipe in `src/lang/execute.rs`'s `source()`, reused unconsumed across every
# job in the sourced file.
#
# Deliberately committed RED: tests/system.rs's own 30-second per-test hang-detection
# timeout (`TEST_TIMEOUT`) means this fails cleanly after 30s rather than hanging the
# suite forever, so it stays as a documented, known-failing repro per this repo's
# convention (see CLAUDE.md: write the repro immediately, even before fixing).
# tests/pty_test_helpers.crush works around this same bug via a single destructuring
# assignment instead of three separate statements.
$script := $(convert $file $("/tmp/source_three_statements_repro_{}":format $(random:integer 1000000000)))
cmd rm "-f" $script
bin:from "echo a\necho b\necho c\n" | bin:to $script
source $script
cmd rm "-f" $script
echo "done"
